[h2]Full changelog[/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug where the reflection of the server room was broken when exiting and entering the server room with the main light on
[*] Fixed a bug where the player's movement was blocked by the cable connector being held;
[*] The notification will not be created if the content is the same as the notification currently being displayed to prevent multiple identical notifications from appearing in sequence;
[*] Fixed a bug where the 3D model of the ZMD River processor was displayed as ZMD Ocean;
[*] Fixed a bug where some non-customizable items in the inventory would open the item selection screen by identifier;
[*] Fixed the collision scale of doors, which could hinder the player's movement in some cases;
[*] Fixed "Reset position" button;
[*] Fixed a bug where equipment, when removed from the server room, was not removed from the network;
[*] Fixed a bug where the LEDs of an Ethernet port remained green even after the cable was removed;
[*] Fixed the position of the rear anchor of the ethernet cable;
[*] Fixed the bug where some cables were not removed when removing equipment from a rack.
[/list]
Alpha access via Ko-Fi: https://ko-fi.com/WebHostSimulator

Discord: https://discord.com/invite/JuyyPbZ

In this update, the focus was on improving the gameplay and game mechanics. I made sure it returned to being as I envisioned it, becoming an immersive game rather than one filled with boring menu screens. I hope you enjoy it, and soon we will have updates with new equipment and services.

[h3]Full changelog[/h3]
[list]
[*] Completely reworked the slot system to use fewer colliders (reduced from 42 colliders to 1 collider per rack) to accept racks and equipment of different sizes and to make the installation more immersive. To remove an object from a slot, you need to hold the right mouse button;
[*] Reworked the door models;
[*] Reworked the cable bay models in the server room;
[*] Optimized global illumination for better performance when active;
[*] Optimized the cable system for better performance and more appropriate visuals;
[*] Removed the operation mode switch (mount/normal);
[*] Removed the exit computer button, now to exit the computer you must hold the right mouse button;
[*] Reworked the player interaction system with an interactive area indicator around the crosshair and holding the right mouse button when available;
[*] Inventory moved to the TAB key;
[*] Minor fixes and improvements.
[/list]

